{
  "slug": "locative-predicate",
  "title": "Locative Predicate",
  "definition": "A [term:predicate] that expresses the location of a referent. Locative predicates often use the same construction as [term:classification-predicate]s or [term:existential-predicate]s, but the predicate phrase is a locative expression (prepositional phrase, locative-case NP, or locative adverb) rather than a noun or adjective. Many languages extend the same construction to other semantic roles such as benefactive and accompaniment.",
  "relatedTerms": ["existential-predicate", "copula", "verbless-clause", "predicate", "classification-predicate"],
